WEBVTT

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:49.750
Himesaka Girls' Academy Koto Club...

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:55.080
"#23    Champions' Resolve"
A super prestigious school that went
to nationals for 10 consecutive years...

00:01:55.080 --> 00:02:00.080
"Unshakable, absolute champions"
that stand unchallenged in Kanagawa...

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.580
That was just who we were.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:06.660
It was our pride... until that day.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.790
The award goes to...

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:14.660
...Kanagawa Prefectural...
Hakuto High School.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.870
What? What happened...?

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.750
It can't be true...

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:22.580
We lost...?

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:24.910
"Himesaka Girls' Academy"

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.290
"Himesaka Girls' Academy"
Club President.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.330
What is it, Wakaba?

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:32.370
To be honest, I don't think
we were inferior to Hakuto.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:35.870
I think their piece turned out to be
more popular with the judges, that's all.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:36.950
Yeah...

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.290
It feels like a fluke.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.540
I disagree.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.700
Yae.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:45.040
Our loss wasn't a fluke.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.160
"There's no way we'll lose
because we're Himesaka."

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.830
I think we lost because that thought
caused us to let our guard down.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:55.370
Yeah, I agree.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.700
We third years want to
get back at Hakuto, too.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.790
But we'll retire after the performance
in Tokyo next week.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:04.410
So we'll entrust it to the first
and second years.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.410
The new club president will be Yae.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.660
Okay!

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:13.160
Going to nationals 11 years in a row
won't be easy, but you can do it!

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.160
Yeah!

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.620
I didn't hear Hakuto's performance.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.120
Right after Tokise finished playing,
I went to see <i>him </i>to complain.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:31.620
I looked down on both Tokise and Hakuto.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.830
Fumi... I...

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:43.830
I feel very... ashamed... of myself.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.290
Don't look so miserable!

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:58.120
It's okay. You're lucky
that you noticed it <i>now</i>.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.000
We can now face the qualifier
thoroughly prepared.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.200
We won't lose next time for sure!

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.330
Fumi...

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.330
Now, brace up!

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.750
We'll practice furiously again
starting tomorrow!

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:09.870
Yep!

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:17.660
Girls! We received the sheet music
for the qualifier piece. Come get it.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.120
"Three Paraphrases"...

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:24.700
I've never played it, but if I
remember correctly, this piece is...

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.160
A-A lot of string-pressing...!

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.910
On top of that, they're sixteenth notes...

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.950
Doesn't the picking in
the second half look crazy?

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.950
And we need to change the tuning a lot!

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:35.540
We have to be in sync with this many people?!

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.830
Shoot...

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.000
I feel super fired up.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.450
Does everyone have it? Okay then,
I'd like to make a suggestion.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:46.750
All these years, every member
played in the qualifier.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:49.620
But you can't win like that anymore.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.620
The era of Himesaka always
being number one is over.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:55.620
So, like we always do for nationals,

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:59.370
I'll choose who will perform by audition.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:01.500
I'll hold the audition one month
prior to the qualifier.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.370
Considering the balance of first koto
and second koto, I'll choose 24 members.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.910
It'll be based on your abilities.
Your year doesn't matter.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.830
I'll choose a team to go to nationals.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.410
What do you think?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:14.750
Okay!

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.750
Okay then. That's decided.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.040
Now, let's start practice. Get ready!

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.620
Hozumi! Why the gloomy face?

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.330
Rui.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:31.750
Well, this piece seems really tough, so...

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.620
It's got a ton of string-pressing,
which I'm not good at.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:36.620
On top of that, 12 members
will be cut by audition.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:40.250
Why are you whining already?!
We still have time.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.500
If we practice like there's
no tomorrow, we'll be fine!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.790
This is the last chance for us second years.
We'll play together on stage!

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:48.620
Yep!

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:52.370
I think we should increase the practice time.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:56.580
What're you saying, Kazusa?
We already have enough practice time.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.750
Really? You can't play it well yet, Wakaba.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.660
What? I've already memorized
the score perfectly.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.870
But the way you play is rough.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.700
Don't act so high-and-mighty!

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.500
I wanna go to nationals for sure!

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:12.450
In order to do so, I wanna do
everything we can do now!

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.620
Hey, you two, calm down.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:19.410
We all want to go to nationals.
Let's work this out. Okay?

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.330
Hozumi...

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.330
Seriously, Kazusa really ticks me off!

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.450
I don't know if she's the daughter
of a grand master or what,

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:33.040
but she's always condescending.
Who does she think she is?

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:37.870
Also, she keeps praising this
Satowa girl from another school.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.450
I bet she looks down on us.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.580
I don't think so.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:45.660
To me, she just looks very desperate.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.500
She seriously wants to go to nationals,

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:50.330
so I'm sure she just spoke a little too harshly.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:52.950
I'm seriously aiming for nationals, too.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:56.000
Of course! I know that.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:01.910
But you two are both first years,
good koto players, and aiming for nationals.

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:05.120
So I thought the two of you
fighting would be a shame.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:07.450
Thank you very much for your concern.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.660
That's sloppy! One more time, from the start!

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.330
Get the tempo right!
Make each sound clear and distinct!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:20.000
Hozumi! You're not pressing
the strings hard at all!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.540
That's just a half tone!

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.950
Not enough! Harder!

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:24.910
--Good practice.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.000
--Good practice.
--Good practice.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:27.790
Bye-bye.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:32.330
Hozumi. Are you gonna keep
practicing by any chance?

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.950
Yeah. My skills aren't good
compared to the others.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:38.910
I can't press strings hard at all, either, so...

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:42.910
There are a lot of string marks on your
left hand. Your fingers look swollen, too.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.450
What? Your hand is like that, too.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.370
Yours is beyond mine.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:50.830
It's embarrassing that only
my fingers look kinda impressive.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:55.000
I have to improve my skills, too.
I'll work hard!

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.910
Um...! Can I practice with you?!

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.910
Of course!

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:06.080
"Himesaka Girls' Academy"

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:08.410
Thus, a month before the qualifier,

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:11.040
we had the audition
to decide the qualifier team.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.830
Next! First koto, Hozumi Tachibana.
Second koto, Rui Natsume!

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:16.830
Okay!

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.910
This is the hardest I've ever practiced.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.790
So I'm sure I'll be okay.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:31.790
Well then... I'll announce
the team for the qualifier.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:33.830
I'll start with the second years.

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:40.540
Makimoto, Yokozawa, Aida, Sakaguchi,
Itofuji, Hara, Nishino, Sato,

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.120
--Watanabe, Oobayashi, Inoue, Ikeda,
Abe, Taniguchi, Iwasaki, and Natsume.

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:47.330
--Wow... Maybe all the second years will be--
--Watanabe, Oobayashi, Inoue, Ikeda,
Abe, Taniguchi, Iwasaki, and Natsume.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.910
That's all. Now, first years.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:55.410
E-Excuse me! All the second years
were called but Hozumi!

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:59.830
Unfortunately, Hozumi isn't
on the team this time.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:03.540
Her hands moved well.
She practiced a lot, too.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:06.620
But her string-pressing was still unstable.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:08.750
That's the reason.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.450
But... But to think that
only Hozumi is left out...

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.540
This is the last qualifier for us second years.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:17.870
That's okay, Rui. It can't be helped.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:22.290
She said it'd be based on our abilities
regardless of our year from the start.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:26.950
I did everything I could. I have no regrets.

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:31.370
Hozumi...

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:34.250
See you tomorrow.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:35.870
Aren't you going home, Hozumi?

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:39.910
No, I'll stay a little longer.

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:42.540
I see. Then I'll see you tomorrow.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:43.450
Yeah.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:57.000
I'm the only second year who
wasn't chosen... How pathetic...

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.750
Hey, Wakaba! That hurts! Let go of me!

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.330
Are you stupid?

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:24.790
If you go talk to her right now, it'll only
make her feel more miserable, right?

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.910
She wasn't chosen because she wasn't good.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:32.120
She couldn't improve enough by the time
of the audition. That's the reality.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:33.200
How dare you say--

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.660
So...

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:38.330
...we'll go to nationals for sure.

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:41.750
If we do, there'll be another
audition before nationals.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:48.370
All we can do for her now is
go to nationals. Am I wrong?

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:52.790
I thought you hated Hozumi.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:55.790
I said she wasn't good,
but I didn't say I hated her.

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:58.290
The only person I hate is you.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.410
Wakaba! I hate you, too!

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:04.410
But just this once, I agree with you!

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:09.080
We're gonna get the ticket to nationals!

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:12.080
We're definitely not gonna let things end here.

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:17.080
We're gonna create the path
that leads us to our next step...

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.750
...for sure...

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:25.580
Program number three.
Himesaka Girls' Academy.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.750
"Three Paraphrases."

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:41.120
Himesaka Girls' Academy.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.200
"Three Paraphrases."

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.750
Are you kidding me?!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.410
Even though there's a lot of
string-pressing and tuning-changing,

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:40.790
they're doing it completely in sync

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.830
while they're playing
sixteenth notes seamlessly!

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:46.500
How can they move their hands like that?

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:50.620
How come no one knocks down
the bridges with this speed?

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:55.450
You girls are amazing!

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:58.450
Keep it up... Keep it up...!

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:02.910
Support member?

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.290
Yes.

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:09.120
When going to nationals,
non-performing members assist, right?

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:12.370
So I was hoping to assist in the same way.

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:17.410
That'd be great... But aren't you
pushing yourself, Hozumi?

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:20.500
I know I'm the one who didn't choose you,
but if it's hard for you--

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.660
It's hard... very hard...

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:23.660
But...

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.830
Hozumi! Good morning!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.540
Rui.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:37.160
Did you hear? We'll be practicing
a lot more from today.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:41.040
I heard that Kazusa and Wakaba
went to ask the advisor directly

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:42.290
even though they don't get along.

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:46.330
What...? I see, those two did...

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:50.290
Hozumi. Make sure you keep practicing...

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.450
...'cause we'll play together at nationals.

00:13:54.620 --> 00:14:00.330
I thought I'd regret it if I just kept
feeling down until the qualifier.

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:04.000
I'm lucky to have friends
who say things like that,

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:08.790
so I'd like to do all I can to spend
this time together with everyone.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:15.000
They haven't messed up at all so far.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.700
Incredible...!

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:21.500
<i>That </i>third movement is coming up soon.

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:45.160
Picking sixteenth notes. Half tones and
whole tones. Irregular string-pressing...

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.580
With this many people? Are they monsters?!

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:51.500
What's this? I didn't realize
kotos could be this incredible...!

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:58.330
We no longer let our guards down thinking,
"Because we're Himesaka."

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.410
We will win!

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:03.250
Incredible...

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.700
Oh... This is...

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:08.200
Yeah, without doubt...

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:16.370
These are the sounds that belong
to those who practice a lot.

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:23.450
Whoa... Very impressive...

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:38.790
Their specialization as a team
has always been staying together,

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.500
but to this extent...?

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:44.870
I never liked their performances before,

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.950
but their performance today was good.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:54.830
Stupid! Stupid Chika!
Why're you casually praising our rival?!

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:56.330
If you praise them, we lose!

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.750
Shut up! What's good is good!

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:01.500
But our performance is better!

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:05.500
Takinami, you bastard!
What're you laughing about?!

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:09.120
Well, I just like this side of you, that's all.

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:14.410
Ah! Mr. Takinami!

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.370
Oh, you're Hakuto's...

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.200
Taishin Yamamoto!

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.830
Mr. Yamamoto. Are you guys moving
to the tuning room now?

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:24.790
Yes. My heart is already pounding so hard.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:30.080
By the way, you instruct
the Hakuto students, right?

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:32.250
Yes, more or less.

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:34.410
Are you a music teacher?

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:39.620
No, I usually teach math,
but I love music, too!

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:43.950
I see... It's amazing that you can
give such a great instruction

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:46.160
when you're not a music teacher.

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:47.000
What?

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:51.370
I heard Hakuto's performance from
the traditional music festival on DVD.

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:54.290
I was blown away by it being so high level.

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:57.040
The piece, as well as the performance,
was perfectly calculated

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:00.160
so that the music would smoothly
come into listeners' hearts.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:05.790
Oh, by the way, who's Miyabi Tojo,
the composer for Hakuto?

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.910
This person creates such high-level pieces,

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:09.870
and yet, no matter how hard I checked--

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:16.580
Did I say something wrong?

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:19.660
Oh, no...! It's not... It's not like that!

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:23.870
N-No one's said that to me before
about the performance and pieces,

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:26.910
so I'm just so happy!

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:27.660
What?

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:31.040
Hey, Mr. Yamamoto! We have to
hurry up or we'll run out time!

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:32.000
Oh... Sorry!

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.120
Now, let's go!

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:39.620
Sorry, Mr. Takinami! If you don't mind,
let's talk sometime soon!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.870
Yes, definitely.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:46.660
Math, huh...? That explains it.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:50.620
No wonder I couldn't find him.

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.000
Kurata.

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:55.910
We need to go to the tuning room now.

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:58.080
Okay.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:01.370
How pathetic, you bunch of scaredy-cats.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:03.540
Hey, that's Chika and the others.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:06.540
I wonder if they're getting ready now.
Do you wanna talk to them?

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:11.370
No, that's okay. I don't wanna
disturb their concentration.

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:13.660
Excuse me. Is that seat taken?

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:15.580
No. Go ahead.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:17.500
Thank you very much.

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:22.660
"Program"

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:23.830
"Tenkyu"

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:27.160
"Tenkyu"
"The heavens... cry"?

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.000
I wonder what this piece is like...

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.910
Ugh! Calm down, my heart!

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:33.910
As expected, everyone's nervous.

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:36.540
I'd better get a grip so I don't catch it, too.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:38.160
Hey!

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:40.620
What's with that scary look?!

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:44.040
Taking the stage is a reward for all the
hard work you've put in until now, right?

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:47.040
We should enjoy it
as much as we can, right?!

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.870
Kurusu...

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:51.120
Your hand is shaking.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:53.160
Sh-Shut up!

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.870
Okay, guys! Let's check
the tuning quickly and practice!

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.500
--But Miss Akira isn't here--

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:05.540
--I'm sorry I'm late!
--But Miss Akira isn't here--

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.040
Miss Akira!

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:10.200
It's rare that you cut it this close.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.830
The roads were busier than I expected.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.910
--Well then, let's--
--M-Miss Akira!

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:19.620
Um... I made this for you, too,
so if you'd like...

00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:23.540
You made it?

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:26.250
I-I-I-It's okay to throw it away!

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:30.620
Thank you very much.
I'm happy to have it... Very happy.

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.370
Come to think of it...

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:35.540
...where's yours?

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:37.290
What? I didn't make one.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:38.410
You didn't?!

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:39.870
Jeez... Then...

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.540
Hey! What're you--

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.790
How's this? Now it's--

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:52.540
Wow! You two are like a couple!

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:53.370
A cou--?!

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.580
Chika. Your handwriting is terrible as usual.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:56.950
Yeah. What terrible handwriting.

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:58.330
What'd you say?!

00:19:58.330 --> 00:19:59.160
I'm jealous...

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:01.620
Stop fooling around and
get on with the preparation.

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:03.790
I know! Dammit!

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:08.000
That was... a happy look on her face... right?

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:14.660
Seriously, Mr. Tsukaji.
I really can't take much more of this.

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:17.790
It's true that Himesaka's
performance was amazing,

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:21.120
but all the schools after them
kinda sound the same to me.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:23.580
You're so hopeless...!

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:26.870
But well, what she said
isn't necessarily wrong.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.790
So far, Himesaka is clearly
the top contender,

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.500
and there's little difference among the rest.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:36.700
Will Himesaka go to nationals
as they've done in other years?

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.250
"Program"
Or...

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.000
"Hakuto High School"

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:42.000
It's about time!

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.290
Get ready to go on stage, everyone!

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.410
Kanzaki. You get ready, too!

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:53.580
How're you doing?

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:54.790
Good.

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:57.580
Hey, it's rare that you say "good."

00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:58.410
Really?

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:03.330
Yeah! You always say stuff like, "normal."

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:07.370
Listen, Mio... The fact is,
Mr. Yamamoto is...

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:08.870
What's wrong?

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:12.620
Photosynthesis.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:16.950
You're like the sun,
so I'm getting power from you.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:22.580
Taishin power!

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:25.080
Now you'll be fine!

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:29.370
You can give your best
performance ever today!

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:30.700
Weirdo.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:37.250
Hey! Mio! Carry your
instrument yourself, okay?!

00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:38.660
You carry it, Club President.

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:40.120
Don't be ridiculous!

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:46.120
I've never seen him smile like that before.

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:49.620
What? Advisor for the koto club?

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:53.160
It's been ten years since then...

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.000
And today is the last day!

00:21:57.370 --> 00:22:01.000
Now... let me hear your performance...

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:06.000
I'll see if your ability to beat Himesaka at the
traditional music festival...

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.290
...is the real deal...

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:53.160
Next time, "Beyond the Right Answer."

00:23:53.160 --> 00:23:54.370
"#24    Beyond the Right Answer"
